E5 Target typed UNKNOWN with exact applied Admission history

Date: 2026-10-07
Base: main@c1257f754a477b39311425177f5d15009a4061eb

Typed UNKNOWN with no next retry work now requires bounded current/first Target Admission signed-envelope images and an immutable RetryPolicySemantic. In the same guarded Store view, both images must match retained APPLIED/OK SYSTEM first results, exact signed-envelope digests and source stamps. The current image must match AttemptBudget Admission hash/stamp and the exact Message obligation; the first image must be attempt 1 for that locator. The policy must match the immutable Schedule binding RetryPolicyRef. Completed attempt, first-admission time, deadline and deterministic jitter are checked against those facts. A mismatch is an integrity failure under Registry section 5 RetryDecision semantics; it does not become an ACKed rejection result.

Ordinary Outcome retains the historical admitted writer identity. The apply-time active Owner is used only to authorize the closed cross-Owner recovery UNKNOWN shape: recovery disposition/code, full UNCERTAIN_HOLD and no next retry. Historical accepted-writer/key and live current Owner snapshot remain obligations of the source authority provider.

